WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.360
But I think you need to do that with
a certain amount of intensity so

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.860
that you really get that first, get
to the first ledge and your climb.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:12.120
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here and
today, I want to talk about learning

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.860
two languages at the same time.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.940
Remember if you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:24.480
Uh, if you're listening, uh, on a podcast
service somewhere, please leave a review.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.860
You can click on the bell
here for notifications.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.220
So I have been learning two
languages at the same time off and

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.019
on for the last couple of years,
that's Arabic and Persian or Farsi.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.810
And I'm about to embark on another
90-Day Challenge, which I also want

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.650
to announce here because at LingQ
we  have these 90-Day Challenges.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.620
We encourage people to commit to
certain goals and follow up with other

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:58.589
LingQ members to see how they're doing
all in sort of a bit of an effort to,

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.780
you know, help each other, motivate
each other, to stay on our tasks.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.500
Now, so I thought about, what do
I want to take on as a challenge?

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.140
And I ended up, I initially
I was going to say, well, I'm

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.529
going to focus just on Arabic.

00:01:12.285 --> 00:01:17.384
And I just, I'm reluctant to leave
Persian even for three months.

00:01:17.384 --> 00:01:20.205
So I ended up saying, well, I
got to do a challenge in both.

00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:24.175
And I have indicated that at
LingQ, that I'm  doing a 90-D ay

00:01:24.195 --> 00:01:26.414
Challenge in both Arabic and Persian.

00:01:27.315 --> 00:01:29.294
So I'll be doing two
languages at the same time.

00:01:29.384 --> 00:01:33.435
In fact, I'll be doing three because
my Arabic is going to be divided

00:01:33.435 --> 00:01:37.544
between standard Arabic, which is
where I spend most of my time, and

00:01:37.544 --> 00:01:40.785
Egyptian Arabic, which I've just
started doing over the last few weeks.

00:01:41.429 --> 00:01:46.110
So it's almost three languages at the
same time, except that EgyptianArabic is

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.750
a part of Arabic as is standard Arabic.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.580
So some thoughts about this, first
of all, I would not recommend

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:57.000
studying two languages at the
same time if you are a beginner.

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:01.110
And remember, I have commented
that language learning is a bit

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:02.820
like an upside down hockey stick.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.720
So you've got the blade of the
stick, which goes up very sharply.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:12.225
And then you have this long shaft
which sort of gradually kind of is

00:02:12.225 --> 00:02:16.155
inclined in an upward direction,
but yeah, you're almost not aware

00:02:16.155 --> 00:02:17.505
that you're making any progress.

00:02:18.135 --> 00:02:24.405
And so during that first steep climb, uh,
where there was a lot of initial success,

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:27.825
all of a sudden, you can say something
where you couldn't say something before

00:02:28.095 --> 00:02:31.545
all of a sudden you understand some
things that you, you know, you didn't

00:02:31.545 --> 00:02:33.055
understand anything when you start.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.820
The language was just noise
at the beginning, and now

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.049
there's some meaning there.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.000
So there's a great sense of achievement.

00:02:39.179 --> 00:02:42.450
It's also a period that first
sort of could be three months,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.970
could be six months, depends on
how difficult the language is.

00:02:45.359 --> 00:02:49.230
You have that sense that, you know,
the vocabulary, the high frequency

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:53.370
vocabulary, repeats so often that you
really do feel as if you're, you're

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.149
acquiring words here and, and, and
getting a sense of the language.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.810
But then once you've passed that
whether it be after three months

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:05.445
or six, because the word frequency,
and I've mentioned this before, the

00:03:05.445 --> 00:03:07.875
word frequency declines so quickly.

00:03:08.295 --> 00:03:11.295
You have this impression that you're
not seeing the words often enough

00:03:11.295 --> 00:03:14.505
to really remember them and you keep
on forgetting them and, and just

00:03:14.505 --> 00:03:19.575
seems like an endless task to build
up the large passive vocabulary that

00:03:19.575 --> 00:03:21.735
you need in order to become fluent.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:29.490
Long intro to say, if you're in that
first stage, the sort of, uh, you know,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:35.250
steep climb, initial period, I would not
recommend trying to do two languages.

00:03:36.329 --> 00:03:37.350
That's been my experience.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:42.019
Other people have different, uh, you know,
experiences, or likes or whatever, but I

00:03:42.019 --> 00:03:46.040
think you need to do that with a certain
amount of intensity so that you really get

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.960
that first get to the first ledge in your

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:49.549
climb.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:53.359
So, but once you're past that
first period, which is...

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:59.520
I'm past it now in both my Persian and
my Arabic, it's that long, long road.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:05.280
And so there, I think it is possible to,
to do two languages at the same time.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.770
And I will share with you my strategy.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:12.540
First of all, on the one hand,
because you're doing two languages,

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.340
you have less of an opportunity
obviously to concentrate on one.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:20.430
So you will learn less quickly.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.779
At least if you had spent...

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.780
if I spent all my time on
Arabic, I would learn Arabic.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:29.219
Because I have done both Arabic and
Persian with a little bit of Turkish

00:04:29.219 --> 00:04:31.620
here that slows me down in my Arabic.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:35.040
However, I end up with two
languages instead of one.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.800
The other thing is that at times,
again, because this long shaft

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.090
where you, you hardly feel you're
making any progress at all, uh, it

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.570
can be a little bit dispiriting.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.320
Uh, I've called it the doldrums, which
is that area of the world where the, the

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.090
wind dies and the ships aren't moving.

00:04:55.125 --> 00:04:58.935
Uh, in the old days when everyone
relied on sale for, for sailing.

00:04:59.505 --> 00:05:05.715
So, uh, in a way, sometimes you're sort
of forcing yourself to do things, to

00:05:05.715 --> 00:05:09.345
learn the language because you want
to learn the language and yet you're,

00:05:09.345 --> 00:05:12.945
you, you don't really feel like you're
making much progress at that time.

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:16.395
I think it's kind of good to
switch from one language to the

00:05:16.395 --> 00:05:19.455
other and back again, because it's
something new, something refreshing.

00:05:20.145 --> 00:05:21.945
You're inspired again.

00:05:21.945 --> 00:05:22.265
When you...

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:25.474
at least that's been my experience
when I go back to language A

00:05:25.495 --> 00:05:27.405
after having been with language B.

00:05:27.825 --> 00:05:32.535
So I think in that period, you can cope
with two languages at the same time.

00:05:33.165 --> 00:05:37.965
Another thing that I think is important
when doing two languages at the same time,

00:05:37.965 --> 00:05:42.165
or even if you're doing one language and
you're in that sort of doldrums period,

00:05:42.165 --> 00:05:44.895
the long shaft, do things that are fun.

00:05:45.375 --> 00:05:51.135
If you are sort of out of a sense of
obligation, forcing yourself to reread

00:05:51.135 --> 00:05:55.845
and reread view the same material
because you keep forgetting it, uh,

00:05:57.045 --> 00:05:58.575
it can be a little bit discouraging.

00:05:58.905 --> 00:06:02.535
On the other hand, uh, I've now
found for example, with my, uh,

00:06:03.165 --> 00:06:05.235
with my, uh, Egyptian Arabic.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:11.195
Uh, my tutor has me on this, um,
the serial on Netflix, Once Upon

00:06:11.195 --> 00:06:14.655
a Time, I think it's called,
uh, what was it called again?

00:06:15.045 --> 00:06:23.255
Uh, I can't remember.

00:06:23.545 --> 00:06:24.720
Uh, geez, what was it called?

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:26.010
I don't know.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:31.320
Anyway, it's, it's, it's an interesting,
very interesting, um, series.

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:33.180
And so it's enjoyable.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:37.125
I don't understand why, but it's
enjoyable and I'm picking up some things.

00:06:37.125 --> 00:06:38.325
So I do a little bit of that.

00:06:38.325 --> 00:06:40.095
I go on and do a little
bit of the mini stories.

00:06:40.095 --> 00:06:44.975
I go do a little bit of standard Arabic,
you know, uh, podcasts out of Al Jazeera.

00:06:45.165 --> 00:06:47.605
So I'm, I'm doing a certain
amount of variety, but I tried

00:06:47.615 --> 00:06:49.185
to do things that I enjoy doing.

00:06:49.785 --> 00:06:54.555
Uh, similarly in Persian, uh, Sahra is
gonna get me some movies on YouTube.

00:06:55.635 --> 00:06:59.474
She's also put in some material, songs
in Persian, which I've been listening to.

00:06:59.474 --> 00:07:03.974
And so if I can vary the kind of
material that I'm listening to, uh,

00:07:04.005 --> 00:07:08.895
things that I enjoy doing, and therefore
I'm not so fussed about how quickly

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.474
I'm improving, the improvement comes.

00:07:11.804 --> 00:07:15.465
You just have to believe that it will
come and don't put pressure on yourself

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:18.224
and wanting to move along more quickly.

00:07:18.224 --> 00:07:23.115
If you sort of say, well, I can
wander into this room, my Arabic

00:07:23.115 --> 00:07:27.435
room for a while, and then I'm going
to go back into my Persian room and

00:07:27.435 --> 00:07:28.844
the flavors are a little different.

00:07:28.844 --> 00:07:30.135
The colors are a little different.

00:07:30.135 --> 00:07:31.965
The content that I'm using
is a little different.

00:07:32.855 --> 00:07:35.465
So I think that's important also.

00:07:35.795 --> 00:07:40.235
Uh, I, uh, I think at this stage it's
important to have a tutor, you know,

00:07:40.235 --> 00:07:44.265
funnily enough, I think a tutor at
the early stage is more difficult

00:07:44.265 --> 00:07:47.085
to take advantage of because you
can't speak, you don't understand.

00:07:47.325 --> 00:07:50.505
You need to invest all that
time in listening and reading.

00:07:50.505 --> 00:07:54.075
And I use the mini stories to get up
to a certain level, or you can actually

00:07:54.375 --> 00:07:58.304
take advantage of a tutor, but once
you're at the level I'm at now, I can

00:07:58.304 --> 00:07:59.565
actually have a conversation with them.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:06.480
And so, uh, I make sure that I have
two conversations a week in Arabic and

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.000
two conversations a week in Persian.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:13.770
And the advantage there is that I'm sort
of committed to being with the tutor.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.440
So again, that kind of propels me forward.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:17.400
I got to do it.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:18.210
I'm there.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:19.130
Uh, I don't...

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.010
I don't prepare.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:23.270
In fact, I shouldn't say I don't
prepare at all for my, for my,

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.400
uh, interactions with my tutors.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.020
They're both excellent tutors.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:27.740
They keep me going.

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:28.340
They ask me question.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:32.850
They ask me about the serial I'm watching
in the case of the Egyptian Arabic.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:37.260
And I know Sahra is a great, uh,
tutor in terms of keeping me going.

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:41.970
And once she's going to recommend
a series on, uh, on YouTube.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:44.610
And we will be talking about that.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:47.189
So I just have to show
up, but I have to show up.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.810
So I'm committed twice a week.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:52.530
Now that's my plan to show up
in each of those languages.

00:08:52.709 --> 00:08:56.459
If I were doing, I could do one week
of one language and one week of the

00:08:56.459 --> 00:09:00.120
other and then similarly I would have a
commitment to show up, but I've decided

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.610
to try to squeeze them into the same week.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:04.350
I don't know how it will all go.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:08.835
And I think that my final bit
of advice is experiment with it.

00:09:09.075 --> 00:09:13.695
I think some people will find it
more enjoyable to do two languages

00:09:13.755 --> 00:09:15.585
at the same time than other people.

00:09:15.585 --> 00:09:17.415
Some people may not enjoy doing that.

00:09:17.415 --> 00:09:19.875
Some people may prefer to
stay with one language.

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:24.405
There is no right way or wrong way or
obligation do the things that you find

00:09:24.405 --> 00:09:28.605
enjoyable, stay with the language, stay
with the process and you will improve.

00:09:28.995 --> 00:09:32.325
And so that's what I have to say on
learning two languages at the same time.

00:09:32.535 --> 00:09:33.365
Thank you for listening.

